			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4398285">
									

<p>This is pretty cool :3 It's absolutely the right level of subtle I feel where when you get it, it hits you like a damn train.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;minor&nbsp;things</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;minor&nbsp;things</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I'm gonna second the auto-playing audio in FILE-(3) being ehhhh (it's also inaccessible for deaf folk: I'd suggest including an actual audio widget here to allow folk to pause it, and an optional transcript of the audio).</p>
<p>&quot;&quot;Soda,&quot;&quot;: it might be a stylistic thing but for me it feels better if the comma is after the &quot; (since the quotation marks feel like they're meant to indicate the name, and the comma isn't part of the name). That said, I believe in American English this is more accepted? So it might just be me?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>if the person identifies as male, female, or any nonbinary gender identity respectively.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I get you're trying to be trans inclusive here (woo!) but the usage of &quot;identifies&quot; here kinda implies a level of &quot;isn't actually but says they are&quot;; I'd suggest something like &quot;if the person is male, female or non-binary respectively&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;SCP-4932's was discovered&quot;: SCP-4932 was</p>
<p>&quot;for presumably three years without losing function&quot;: I'm not sure if there's something I'm missing but I don't get why they think it's been there for 3 years?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Several hollow shells created out steel and concrete can be seen nearby the location of SCP-4932's discovery</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&#8230;created out of steel&#8230;seen near the location&#8230;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It is unknown how the message written in permanent marker written on SCP-4932 managed to survive in these conditions.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>double usage of written; &quot;not known&quot; feels a little better than &quot;unknown&quot; here too</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

