<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>so it seems like, uh, &quot;the child&quot; causes things to be taken out of reality? or things it observes have never existed through a gradual fading effect? like how some people knew about johnathan vaugely, like fragments of memories, and others completely forgot about him? also how it mentions how cars would take 3 days to disappear, and the continent took 5 months to disappear and resulted in trillions of gallons of water displacement. overall, i think it was pretty cool, like, having these people whose goal is to figure out how to kill it before it renders all of humanity extinct (tidal action through the moon disappearing, and just general extinction of most life because of the sun extinguishing. one question i have is: are they aware of their effect? i feel like that's the real punch of the article, is that like, they still believe the things they made disappear exist. like, how the phone reveals their view of reality(?) is really cool. satisfying article, i really enjoyed it (also i probably entirely missed the point of the article haha)</p>
